  "id": "DrugBank_DB01053 - MONDO_21680",
  "verbalization": "Benzylpenicillin is implicated in the treatment of Streptococcal Infection through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Benzylpenicillin is linked to Streptococcal Infection via Procaine Benzylpenicillin, which is indicated in multiple contexts, including Pinta Disease and Asymptomatic Neurosyphilis. These conditions, in turn, are associated with Procaine Benzylpenicillin, indicating a potential role in the pathophysiology of Streptococcal Infection. The shared use of Procaine Benzylpenicillin across different indications suggests a possible mechanism of action that targets bacterial pathogens, possibly through inhibition of cell wall synthesis. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential dependency on Procaine Benzylpenicillin as a mediator in the relationship between Benzylpenicillin and Streptococcal Infection, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
